{
  "_comment": [
    "DEVELOPMENT telemetry credentials for this checkout. GITIGNORED, and listed in",
    ".claude/hooks/outbound-guard.py's PRIVATE_FILES so no value here can reach a PR body, an",
    "issue comment or a commit message.",
    "",
    "DO NOT FILL THIS IN BY HAND -- run `make telemetry-local`, which fetches the two _DEV",
    "values from GitHub repository variables and writes this file 0600. GitHub is the single",
    "source of truth for every credential; the working copy is a cache, never an origin. This",
    "example exists to document the SHAPE, and to say what deliberately is not in it.",
    "",
    "The names end in _dev and that is load-bearing rather than tidy. The app derives the",
    "`environment` it reports from WHICH credential pair it was compiled with",
    "(telemetry::sender::ENVIRONMENT), so a build fed from this file labels itself",
    "`development` and cannot label itself anything else. Neutral names would let a local",
    "build report as production while sending to the dev project -- the label and the",
    "destination disagreeing, which is the one failure a provenance-derived field must not have.",
    "",
    "The PRODUCTION pair is NOT here and must never be: it exists only as the repository",
    "variables PLX_SENTRY_DSN and PLX_POSTHOG_KEY, injected by .github/workflows/release.yml.",
    "Supplying both pairs to one build is a compile error, not a warning.",
    "",
    "There is NO sentry_auth_token here either, and that is the mechanism rather than a",
    "policy: `gh` cannot read a secret's value, and the only consumer -- sentry-cli, uploading",
    "debug files -- runs in CI. So the one credential that can read and delete the project has",
    "no reason to sit on a laptop. If you ever need to upload by hand, mint a SECOND",
    "organization token for that consumer; never copy the CI one.",
    "",
    "The two values that are here are WRITE-ONLY ingest credentials, publishable by design --",
    "any binary that sends anything must carry them, and `strings` finds them in every build."
  ],
  "sentry_dsn_dev": "https://<public_key>@oNNNNNN.ingest.de.sentry.io/<project_id>",
  "posthog_key_dev": "phc_...",
  "sentry_org": "<org-slug>",
  "sentry_project": "<project-slug>",
  "posthog_host": "https://eu.i.posthog.com"
}
